2026-11-18 22:29:58 - Agent_20261118222919 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed CodeQL findings for unsafe pickle deserialization (CWE-502) in Pydantic. Found 2 confirmed true positive vulnerabilities:

1. pydantic/v1/parse.py:42 - pickle.loads() called with untrusted data when allow_pickle=True
2. pydantic/deprecated/parse.py:54 - pickle.loads() called with untrusted data when allow_pickle=True

Both vulnerabilities allow arbitrary code execution through malicious pickle payloads when the allow_pickle parameter is explicitly set to True. While the default is False (safe-by-default design), the vulnerability exists for callers who enable pickle deserialization. The deprecated status of these functions does not eliminate the risk for existing code.
